+
+One caveat worth knowing: `apparent_encoding` reads `r.content`, so the fallback only works cleanly when the content has already been buffered (i.e. a non-`stream=True` request, or after you've touched `r.content`/`r.text`). For a genuinely streamed response with no declared charset, there is no body to sample for detection without consuming the stream — this matches upstream Requests' behaviour.
