+
+## What was wrong
+
+In `requests/utils.py`, `stream_decode_response_unicode` — which `Response.iter_content(decode_unicode=True)` delegates to — bailed out and yielded raw bytes whenever `r.encoding is None`:
+
+```python
+if r.encoding is None:
+    for item in iterator:
+        yield item
+    return
+```
+
+An `application/json` body has no `charset` in its `Content-Type`, so `Response.encoding` is `None`. `Response.text` handles that by falling back to `r.apparent_encoding` (chardet), but the streaming path never did — hence `bytes` from `iter_content(decode_unicode=True)` vs `str` from `.text`.
+
+## The fix
+
+Use `r.apparent_encoding` when `r.encoding` is `None`, and only fall back to raw bytes if detection itself fails (`None`). The fallback loop is kept Python 2.6/2.7 compatible (no `yield from`).
